      <title>With Westinghouse, US's Nuclear Champion Follows an Old Playbook</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-09-22/with-westinghouse-us-s-nuclear-champion-follows-an-old-playbook</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">cfeccc2467db35271495d3ac</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:30:04 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>For all the buzz of small modular reactors and artificial intelligence hyperscalers, the rebirth of the US nuclear power industry looks increasingly old-school. Westinghouse Electric Co. is reportedly set to soon file publicly for a $50 billion initial public offering, and it is no startup. Westinghouse supplied the reactor for America’s first large-scale civilian nuclear power station and traces back to 1886.</description>
